{"name":"Army Issue Green","hex":"#838254","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"army","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, highly organized military force, concerned mainly with ground (rather than air or naval) operations.","Used absolutely for that entire branch of the armed forces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/army"},{"term":"issue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action or an instance of flowing or coming out, an outflow, particularly:\n A movement of soldiers towards an enemy, a sortie.\n The outflow of a bodily fluid, particularly  in abnormal amounts.","A movement of soldiers towards an enemy, a sortie."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow out, to proceed from, to come out or from.","To rush out, to sally forth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/issue"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Army","blocks":[{"text":"An army, ground force or land force is an armed force that fights primarily on land. In the broadest sense, it is the land-based military branch, service branch, or armed service of a nation or country. It may also include aviation assets by possessing an army aviation component. Within a national military force, the word army may also mean a field army."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/250th_United_States_Army_Birthday_Parade_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_June_14%2C_2025_-_262.jpg/330px-250th_United_States_Army_Birthday_Parade_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_June_14%2C_2025_-_262.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army","wikidata":"Q37726"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg/500px-The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg/1280px-The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passe